Creating Boot Init Scripts and System Startup Configuration

1. Create directory structure for init scripts and service runlevels:

`mkdir -p /etc/init.d`
`mkdir -p /etc/rc.d`

2. Create the primary boot initialization script (/etc/init.d/rcS):

cat << 'EOF' > /etc/init.d/rcS
#!/bin/sh
# Early system initialization script

echo "Mounting kernel virtual filesystems..."
mount -t proc proc /proc
mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev
mkdir -p /dev/pts /run
mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /run

echo "Initializing system hostname..."
if [ -r /etc/hostname ]; then
    hostname -F /etc/hostname
fi

echo "Mounting local filesystems..."
mount -a

echo "Starting system logging..."
syslogd
klogd

echo "System initialization complete."
EOF

3. Make the rcS boot script executable:

`chmod +x /etc/init.d/rcS`

4. Symlink BusyBox init to /sbin/init:

`ln -sf /bin/busybox /sbin/init`

5. Create /etc/inittab to control system runlevels and shell spawning:

cat << 'EOF' > /etc/inittab
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::askfirst:-/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
EOF

chmod 644 /etc/inittab
